# GazaOS Android Source Manifest

GazaOS is a **HyperOS-Hybrid Lite AOSP 16.2** custom ROM combining upstream stability from **Lunaris-AOSP**, **crDroid**, and **LineageOS** with **GazaOS** system styling, **Gaza Lab**, modular Quick Settings, lightweight HyperOS 4 media, and a **Free Palestine** humanitarian solidarity mission.

## Quick Sync

Initialize the GazaOS 16.2 manifest:

```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/GazaOS/android -b 16.2 --git-lfs
```

Sync source trees cleanly (shallow, current branch, no tags):

```bash
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

## Device Trees

GazaOS core ROM repositories stay decoupled from device-specific trees. Place your device, vendor, kernel, and hardware trees under `.repo/local_manifests/` or via `breakfast <codename>` before building.

## Lite Build Configuration Flags

Heavy add-on packages are **disabled by default** (`?= false`) in `vendor/lineage/config/lunaris.mk` to keep system images small and fast. Override any of these in your device makefile (`BoardConfig.mk` / `lineage_<device>.mk`) as needed:

| Flag | Default | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `TARGET_LOW_END_BLUR` | `true` | Lightweight `kawase_darkmoon` blur algorithm |
| `TARGET_INCLUDE_AX_THEME_STORE` | `false` | Optional theme store app |
| `TARGET_INCLUDE_BATTERY_STATS` | `false` | Optional battery stats viewer app |
| `TARGET_INCLUDE_GAMESPACE` | `false` | Optional GameSpace overlay app |
| `TARGET_INCLUDE_FREEFORM` | `false` | Optional LMO Freeform & sidebar |
| `TARGET_INCLUDE_OMNISTYLE` | `false` | Optional OmniStyle header packs |
| `TARGET_INCLUDE_V4A` | `true` (`!= true` to exclude) | Set `TARGET_EXCLUDE_V4A := true` to omit ViPER4AndroidFX |
| `TARGET_EXCLUDE_HYPEROS_WALLPAPERS` | `false` | Set `true` to omit `GazaOSWallpapers` |
| `WITH_GMS` | `false` | Set `true` to bundle Pixel GMS suite |

## Build

```bash
. build/envsetup.sh
lunch lineage_<device_codename>-bp4a-user
m bacon
```

## Device Tree Integration & Overlay Guide

### Maintainer & Device Props

Define in your device's `lineage_<codename>.mk` (`PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES`):

```makefile
PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
    ro.gazaos.maintainer=YourName \
    ro.gazaos.device=<codename>
```

### About Phone Device Info Strings (Overlay)

`GazaOsAboutInfoPreferenceController` automatically populates hardware summary fields on first boot, or you can override them cleanly in your device tree overlay (`overlay/<device>/packages/apps/Settings/res/values/lunaris_strings.xml`):

```xml
<resources>
    <string name="lunaris_device_message" translatable="false">Redmi Note 12 5G</string>
    <string name="lunaris_processor_code_message" translatable="false">Snapdragon 4 Gen 1</string>
    <string name="lunaris_battery_type_message" translatable="false">5000 mAh · 33W Fast Charge</string>
    <string name="lunaris_screen_message" translatable="false">6.67" AMOLED · 120 Hz</string>
</resources>
```

Reference example overlay commit/file from upstream base:
- [NTSettingsResTarget/res/values/lunaris_strings.xml](https://github.com/Pong-Development/device_nothing_Pong/blob/luna/overlay/pong/NTSettingsResTarget/res/values/lunaris_strings.xml)

### Additional Device & Display Flags

```makefile
# UDFPS & GMS
TARGET_CUSTOM_UDFPS := true
WITH_GMS := true
WITH_GMS_COMMS_SUITE := false
WITH_PIXEL_LAUNCHER := false
TARGET_USE_MAPS := true
TARGET_USE_FILES := true
TARGET_USE_GPHOTOS := false
TARGET_USE_WALLPAPERS := false

# Display & SurfaceFlinger tuning
USE_REALITY_ENGINE := true
SURFACE_FLINGER_BOOST := true
$(call soong_config_set,surfaceflinger,frame_rate_category_high,120)
$(call soong_config_set,surfaceflinger,frame_rate_category_min,60)
```

To cap AOD & Ambient Display refresh rate via SystemUI overlay (`overlay/.../frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml`):

```xml
<!-- Preferred max refresh rate at AOD & Ambient Display, if supported by the display. -->
<integer name="config_aodMaxRefreshRate">60</integer>
```
